Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:43:59 +0530
Subject: bind the page intelligence service for a frame

GN half only. This is the dependency edge that links TaffyGo's browser-process
code into //chrome/browser; the call-site edit in
chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc that this patch's specification describes
lands in this same commit when it is written.

The edge is what makes the C++ compile and link at all, and it is also how
TaffyGo's native code reaches the APK: an Android APK's Java side carries
assert_no_native_deps, so native code arrives through libchrome rather than
through the product target's deps.

The specification did not mention this half. Every .cc-editing specification in
the queue names its call site and omits the deps edge that resolves the symbol,
because they were written without a checkout to compile against.

Rebase risk: low. One line in a long sorted list.

Needed by: WP-M2-02.

Taffy-Patch: 0006

diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
index e1d0017fc823e..01eeda29e78ad 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -2469,6 +2469,7 @@ source_set("browser") {
     "//components/page_content_annotations/core",
     "//components/supervised_user/core/browser:device_parental_controls",
     "//components/supervised_user/core/browser:synthetic_field_trial_delegate",
+    "//taffy/browser",
     "//components/visibility_timer",
 
